              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for sugar, then the Urdu for salt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: مرچ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مرچ — mirch — \"chilli, pepper\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مرچ (mirch) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from maricca, \"peppercorn\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 9875). It is a variant CDIAL reconstructs beside Sanskrit marīca, \"peppercorn\", which it takes from an Austroasiatic language. When the chilli came to India, it took the name of black pepper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
